ee — particularly whether a progressive Democrat or an election-denier Republican tops the ticket — could quickly move this forecast.", "confidence": "low", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Wisconsin remains one of the most evenly divided states in the country, with an even partisan lean and a recent history of razor-thin presidential margins. With the incumbent term-limited, neither party starts with an incumbency advantage, and the race is genuinely open on both sides.\n\nNo general-election polls, expert ratings, or market prices are available yet, so the forecast rests on fundamentals alone, which point to a dead-even contest. Recent coverage has focused on the nominating fights — Democratic worries about a progressive nominee and questions about primary polling, plus Republican concerns over election-denier candidates — rather than the general election itself. Until real matchup data arrives, a coin-flip race with unusually wide uncertainty is the honest read.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.498, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.4982, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.5145, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4971, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.5003, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.498, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.5067, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.5039, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.5006, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.4971, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.4956, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.4974, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.4993, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.5029, "margin": 0.0}]}